<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BCP exercises bond conversion.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BCP exercises bond conversion.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Comercial Portugues said on Wednesday that it had issued 13.314 million new shares after the exercise of rights on an issue of convertible bonds.</p>
<p>The operation, which was carried out on Wednesday, would raise the company's capital to 150 billion escudos from 136.69 billion, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The convertible bonds were issued following the approval of the board of directors in March 1992.</p>
<p>($1=173 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
